WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.401
Let's turn now to the Justice

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:02.235
Department's probe.

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:03.803
This is a separate investigation

00:00:03.803 --> 00:00:05.038
into classified documents

00:00:05.038 --> 00:00:05.839
found at Mar a Lago.

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:06.473
The Washington

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:07.974
Post yesterday

00:00:07.974 --> 00:00:08.808
reporting this,

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.210
that federal investigators

00:00:10.210 --> 00:00:11.911
have, quote, amassed fresh evidence

00:00:11.911 --> 00:00:14.147
pointing to possible obstruction

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.482
by former President Trump.

00:00:15.482 --> 00:00:15.682
Here's

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:16.683
what The Post is reporting,

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:17.851
that investigators now

00:00:17.851 --> 00:00:20.820
suspect the boxes of classified documents

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:21.855
were moved

00:00:21.855 --> 00:00:23.790
from a storage area at Mar a Lago.

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.724
This is after

00:00:24.724 --> 00:00:26.192
and this this matters the timing

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:27.727
after the DOJ

00:00:27.727 --> 00:00:28.828
served a subpoena

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:30.997
to recover those documents from Florida

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.133
and that Trump personally,

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:35.201
investigators believe, examined

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.003
at least some of those boxes again

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:38.671
after the subpoena.

00:00:38.671 --> 00:00:41.174
Trump's team only returned some documents

00:00:41.408 --> 00:00:42.642
with classified markings.

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:43.209
An FBI

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:43.710
search at Mar

00:00:43.710 --> 00:00:44.911
a Lago would later find more

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.312
than 100 classified items

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:47.981
that were not turned over,

00:00:47.981 --> 00:00:49.783
including top secret documents.

00:00:49.783 --> 00:00:51.051
The Post reports investigators

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.085
have obtained emails

00:00:52.085 --> 00:00:53.019
and text messages

00:00:53.019 --> 00:00:54.854
of a former Trump staffer,

00:00:54.854 --> 00:00:56.523
and they give a detailed understanding

00:00:56.523 --> 00:00:57.357
of what was happening

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.558
during those months.

00:00:58.558 --> 00:00:59.192
At Mar a lot.

00:00:59.192 --> 00:01:00.627
But more on that as we get it.

00:01:00.627 --> 00:01:01.728
Now, let's get perspective

00:01:01.728 --> 00:01:02.429
on what's happening,

00:01:02.429 --> 00:01:03.596
especially here in New York.

00:01:03.596 --> 00:01:04.798
CNN senior legal analyst

00:01:04.798 --> 00:01:05.899
and a former assistant U.S.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:07.267
attorney for the Southern District

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:08.001
of New York, Mr.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:09.636
Elie Hoenig. Joins us now.

00:01:09.636 --> 00:01:10.603
And we should point out

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.272
that he also knows Manhattan D.A.

00:01:12.272 --> 00:01:14.207
Alvin Bragg personally here.

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.608
So we just want to disclose that.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:16.142
Good morning to you.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.410
Let's start with New York and Diamond

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.511
we're going to see this week.

00:01:18.511 --> 00:01:19.312
What are we learning about

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:20.647
the charges that he might be facing?

00:01:20.647 --> 00:01:21.047
Basically,

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.215
what's in the indictment, right.

00:01:22.215 --> 00:01:23.817
So we've not seen the indictment yet,

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:24.617
but we're getting really

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:26.619
important indicators that give us a sense

00:01:26.619 --> 00:01:27.687
of what could be in there.

00:01:27.687 --> 00:01:29.189
First of all, Don, on Friday,

00:01:29.189 --> 00:01:30.023
the judge in this case

00:01:30.023 --> 00:01:31.591
issued the first official

00:01:31.591 --> 00:01:32.659
order in the case,

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:33.660
basically just saying

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:34.260
Alvin Bragg,

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:35.662
the D.A., can disclose

00:01:35.662 --> 00:01:36.796
that there's an indictment.

00:01:36.796 --> 00:01:38.164
It will be unsealed on Tuesday.

00:01:38.164 --> 00:01:39.799
But this is really an important moment

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.634
because we saw for the first time

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.502
the case captured

00:01:42.502 --> 00:01:43.937
people of the state of New York

00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:46.172
against Donald J. Trump defendant.

00:01:46.339 --> 00:01:47.674
This is real.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.242
We also learned over the weekend

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:50.176
that there will be at least

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:51.945
one felony charge in this indictment.

00:01:51.945 --> 00:01:52.912
There better be, by the way,

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:54.447
if this is just a bunch of misdemeanors.

00:01:54.447 --> 00:01:54.747
The D.A.

00:01:54.747 --> 00:01:55.982
is going to have some serious questions

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:56.282
to answer.

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:57.650
But here's what that could mean.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.252
It looks like some of the charges

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:01.054
will relate to falsification

00:02:01.054 --> 00:02:02.021
of business records.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:03.990
The idea is they falsely log

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:05.525
these payments as attorneys fees.

00:02:05.525 --> 00:02:07.026
But that would just be a misdemeanor.

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:08.761
The less serious type of charge

00:02:08.761 --> 00:02:10.196
with a one year maximum.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.131
The dividing line

00:02:11.131 --> 00:02:12.665
between a misdemeanor and a felony,

00:02:12.665 --> 00:02:14.200
by the way, is one year.

00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:15.068
If it's one year or less,

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:16.569
it's a misdemeanor as the max.

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:17.837
And if it's above one year,

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.805
then it's a felony.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.406
How could they make this a felony

00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:21.241
if they can tie

00:02:21.241 --> 00:02:22.342
those business records

00:02:22.342 --> 00:02:23.843
to some other crime,

00:02:23.843 --> 00:02:25.245
to some second crime?

00:02:25.245 --> 00:02:26.513
And the theory here

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:27.480
is that second crime

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.682
could be a campaign finance violation.

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:31.151
If prosecutors charge

00:02:31.151 --> 00:02:32.685
and prove that it's a Class

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:33.453
E felony,

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:33.987
the lowest

00:02:33.987 --> 00:02:35.588
level of felony in New York state,

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.457
which has a maximum of four years.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:38.491
And finally, Don,

00:02:38.491 --> 00:02:39.626
we know from our reporting

00:02:39.626 --> 00:02:41.060
from John Miller and others here

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.629
that the indictment is expected to have.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:43.830
34 counts.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.464
That's a lot.

00:02:44.464 --> 00:02:45.832
But each individual

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:46.833
entry in the business

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.001
records could be its own count.

00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:48.368
You've heard

00:02:48.368 --> 00:02:49.135
a lot of the Trump

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:50.436
folks out this week in the attorney

00:02:50.436 --> 00:02:51.337
saying that they're going to fight this,

00:02:51.337 --> 00:02:52.939
they're going to seek to dismiss this.

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.073
What kind of legal tactics

00:02:54.073 --> 00:02:55.275
will they use to do that?

00:02:55.275 --> 00:02:56.342
They're not playing this one

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:57.177
very close to the vest.

00:02:57.177 --> 00:02:58.478
They spent a lot of the weekend

00:02:58.478 --> 00:02:59.412
talking to Dana Bash

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.014
and others about their strategy.

00:03:01.014 --> 00:03:03.082
They are going to argue that legally

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.250
we are in state court here

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.218
in New York state court.

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:06.953
You cannot charge a violation

00:03:06.953 --> 00:03:08.388
of a federal election law.

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.956
This is a presidential election

00:03:09.956 --> 00:03:10.924
under state law.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:12.692
And if they do that, by the way,

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:15.028
they could knock out this

00:03:15.028 --> 00:03:16.262
because that other crime

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.697
is the federal election violation,

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.532
leaving them with only a misdemeanor.

00:03:19.532 --> 00:03:20.166
So that's going to be

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.668
a really important argument.

00:03:21.668 --> 00:03:22.535
We also know

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:23.102
from listening

00:03:23.102 --> 00:03:24.304
to Trump's lawyers this weekend,

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:25.004
they're going to argue

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:26.539
there was no intent to defraud here.

00:03:26.539 --> 00:03:28.675
Meaning in most business records cases,

00:03:28.675 --> 00:03:30.743
somebody takes a record, falsifies it,

00:03:30.910 --> 00:03:31.978
gives it to somebody else

00:03:31.978 --> 00:03:33.880
in order to steal money.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:34.747
That's not the case here.

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.282
It's a little different scenario.

00:03:36.282 --> 00:03:38.017
They're going to argue that as well.

00:03:38.017 --> 00:03:38.518
Trump's team

00:03:38.518 --> 00:03:39.352
is also going to argue

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.620
statute of limitations,

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.889
meaning you typically have five years

00:03:42.889 --> 00:03:44.257
from the time of felonies committed

00:03:44.257 --> 00:03:45.525
to charge it, two years

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.226
for a misdemeanor.

00:03:46.226 --> 00:03:46.926
Now we're beyond

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.528
both of those time periods.

00:03:48.528 --> 00:03:49.329
However,

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.530
they are going to be rescued here

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.631
because prosecutors

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:52.265
are going to be rescued

00:03:52.265 --> 00:03:53.299
because there's a New York law

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.535
that says you can pause that time period

00:03:55.535 --> 00:03:56.502
when someone's living

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:57.971
continuously out of state.

00:03:57.971 --> 00:03:59.372
Trump has lived in the White House

00:03:59.372 --> 00:04:00.473
and Mar a Lago.

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:01.407
And then finally,

00:04:01.407 --> 00:04:03.243
I am certain that Trump's team

00:04:03.243 --> 00:04:04.410
and they've more than signaled

00:04:04.410 --> 00:04:05.612
this is going to argue

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:06.913
selective prosecution.

00:04:06.913 --> 00:04:07.513
They're going to say

00:04:07.513 --> 00:04:08.848
he's been singled out

00:04:08.848 --> 00:04:09.949
for political purposes.

00:04:09.949 --> 00:04:11.317
That's a really difficult argument

00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.253
to succeed using their John Edwards

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.188
argument, right? Yes. This case. Right.

00:04:15.188 --> 00:04:15.822
What about the judge?

00:04:15.822 --> 00:04:17.624
Because Trump has talked about the judge.

00:04:17.624 --> 00:04:18.658
What about the judge in this case?

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:19.158
We know.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:20.059
So the judge here,

00:04:20.059 --> 00:04:20.960
Juan Mershon, by the way,

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.761
let me just point out

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:24.097
this is called New York Supreme Court.

00:04:24.130 --> 00:04:25.231
A little bit confusing.

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.599
That's what they call the trial

00:04:26.599 --> 00:04:28.067
level court here in New York.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:29.702
The judge is a former prosecutor.

00:04:29.702 --> 00:04:31.537
He was with the DA's office, same office.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.872
It's prosecuting this case.

00:04:32.872 --> 00:04:33.873
And the AG's office

00:04:33.873 --> 00:04:34.807
let me say, nothing

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.643
unusual or inappropriate about that.

00:04:36.643 --> 00:04:38.711
Many judges are former prosecutors.

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:39.846
He's been on the bench

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:42.348
since 2006, best known before this

00:04:42.515 --> 00:04:44.050
because he presided over the case

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.151
against Allen Weisselberg,

00:04:45.151 --> 00:04:46.052
who pled guilty

00:04:46.052 --> 00:04:48.087
and the trial of the Trump Organization.

00:04:48.121 --> 00:04:49.389
Trump's lawyers, by the way.

00:04:49.389 --> 00:04:50.356
They object to this

00:04:50.356 --> 00:04:52.191
because the way this judge got put on

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.226
this case is prosecutors

00:04:53.226 --> 00:04:55.528
said it's related to these cases,

00:04:55.528 --> 00:04:56.996
so he should get it as opposed

00:04:56.996 --> 00:04:58.264
to just going to the wheel

00:04:58.264 --> 00:04:59.165
for random assignment.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:00.199
Watch for Trump's lawyers

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.567
to challenge that and say

00:05:01.567 --> 00:05:03.202
this should not be related to that.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:05.138
We should get a randomly assigned judge.

00:05:05.138 --> 00:05:06.239
And finally, don,

00:05:06.239 --> 00:05:07.106
the judge has to make

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:08.675
his first really big decision

00:05:08.675 --> 00:05:09.842
probably today

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:11.678
about whether he'll allow cameras

00:05:11.678 --> 00:05:12.245
in the courtroom

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.313
for tomorrow's proceeding.

00:05:13.313 --> 00:05:14.914
We at CNN are part of

00:05:14.914 --> 00:05:16.249
a group of media outlets

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.550
that have asked the judge,

00:05:17.550 --> 00:05:19.519
let us see it open up the courtroom.

00:05:19.519 --> 00:05:20.753
It's a public proceeding.

00:05:20.753 --> 00:05:21.654
Let the cameras in.

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:22.855
He'll have to decide that soon.

00:05:22.855 --> 00:05:24.257
Do you think that will happen?

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.291
You know, he has a history

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.592
of not allowing cameras in,

00:05:26.592 --> 00:05:27.493
but given the level

00:05:27.493 --> 00:05:28.861
of public interest here,

00:05:28.861 --> 00:05:30.096
I don't see how he says no.

00:05:30.096 --> 00:05:31.531
I think it's I think he look,

00:05:31.531 --> 00:05:32.799
if I can opinion for a second,

00:05:32.799 --> 00:05:34.300
he should let cameras in

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.468
because the public interest in

00:05:35.468 --> 00:05:37.103
this is through the roof. Really.

00:05:37.103 --> 00:05:37.570
All right.

00:05:37.570 --> 00:05:39.072
Ellie Hoenig, thank you very much.

00:05:39.072 --> 00:05:39.672
Appreciate that.

